# (#218) The interrogated call-local is bound by its FIRST write in the call:
# a read (or a `prev of`) before it walks the chain to the module binding
# (VM: 1, then the module tape's prev), a read after it sees the call-local
# (0.25), and the second call starts unbound again (the frame env is fresh)
# while the tape carries both calls' writes (prev 0.25 on call two). A
# sibling function reading the name during the call sees the MODULE value.
z is 1.0
z is 2.0
define w() as:
    return z
define u() as:
    print of z
    print of (prev of z)
    z is 0.25
    print of z
    print of (w of [])
    return prev of z
print of (u of [])
print of z
print of (u of [])
print of z
